Limit: Claude Code 2.1.283 holds a cross-session message for the owner's approval when the receiving session bypasses permission prompts and the sender attests no permission mode; the daemon's wake is such a message, so a wake written straight to the session's messaging socket stopped starting a turn, observed on two canonical CTO sessions
Limit: the daemon accepts a wake endpoint only directly in its state directory, so the proxy sits beside the session's messaging socket and passes the daemon's endpoint checks exactly when that socket would, with none of them loosened
Limit: the daemon's wake reads no reply and counts as delivered once its frame is written, so a forward to the session that fails after that shows only on the relay's stderr (attach: wake forward failed <shape>), never in the daemon's wake classification
Limit: a relay killed before it closes leaves its acp-wake-proxy-*.sock file in the state directory; nothing sweeps it
Ruled-out: attesting a permission mode from the daemon's own wake client | rejected because that attestation is undocumented
Ruled-out: pressing the held-message dialog on the owner's behalf | rejected because it is forbidden
Ruled-out: a wake-proxy/ subdirectory of the state root for the proxy socket | the daemon refuses an endpoint whose parent is not exactly its state directory, so the proxy sits beside the session's socket rather than in a directory of its own
Ruled-out: refusing a role_wake_endpoint_register call for any path other than the session's own messaging socket | the daemon already decides which endpoints it accepts and the proxy forwards only to the environment's socket, so such a call is forwarded as it arrived rather than refused
Warn: the wake proxy must forward only the constant ROLE_WAKE_FRAME, byte for byte, and only to CLAUDE_CODE_MESSAGING_SOCKET: a message from the session's own child bypasses the hold, so any other byte or target makes the proxy a way to type into the session on the owner's behalf
Warn: WAKE_FRAME in src/cli/attach-relay.ts is a copy of ROLE_WAKE_FRAME in src/mcp/role-conversation.ts; change both together, and tests/process/relay-wake-proxy.test.ts fails when they drift
Warn: a test that runs the relay's CLI entry from inside a Claude Code session inherits that session's CLAUDE_CODE_MESSAGING_SOCKET and CLAUDE_CODE_MESSAGING_TOKEN, so the relay would open a proxy beside the real session's socket; clear both variables first
Unverified: live Claude Code delivering the relay's auth-line wake without holding it was not observed; the tests drive a recording stand-in for the session's messaging socket
