Limit: no lstat sees what connect resolved: a messaging-socket name moved elsewhere just for the forward's connect and moved back before the look after it passes both looks; the owner-only directory leaves that move to this uid
Ruled-out: renaming only the client ids that collide with an outstanding relay id, rather than every client request id | the late answer to a relay request whose wait timed out has no waiter left and would still reach a client request reusing that id
Ruled-out: pinning the session socket's inode when the proxy opens, rather than checking afresh at each wake | a restart of the session's messaging server recreates the socket under a new inode and would be refused for the rest of the relay's life
Warn: inspectWakeTarget in src/cli/attach-relay.ts copies the endpoint checks of #validateEndpointPath in src/mcp/role-conversation.ts by name and order; with the proxy registered the daemon checks only the proxy, so a check added on the daemon side must be added to inspectWakeTarget too or the messaging token can go to a socket the daemon would refuse
Warn: the relay's own requests on a daemon connection must carry string ids: every client request leaves under a relay-counted number and its answer returns under the client's id, and a client message that names a request id (notifications/cancelled) must be renamed the same way
Unverified: endpoint-owner-mismatch and a name swapped between the two looks are exercised only through a mocked lstatSync in tests/process/relay-wake-proxy.test.ts; no socket owned by another uid and no real rename race was tested
