Limit: the relay sends a request of its own on a live daemon link only while its wake proxy listens, so with no proxy there is no relay id for a client id to collide with, and every line in either direction passes byte for byte as before the proxy existed
Ruled-out: keying the id renaming on the messaging variables being present, rather than on the wake proxy listening | a complete environment whose socket the proxy may not forward to opens no proxy, and renaming there would change the client's bytes with no proxy to protect
Warn: r-1057r1r2target's Warn that every client request leaves under a relay-counted number holds only while the wake proxy listens: with no proxy the relay renames nothing, and a request read before the proxy listened keeps the client's own id until it is answered
Warn: nextUpstreamId and nextInternalId in src/cli/attach-relay.ts skip every id that a request sent under the client's own id before the proxy opened still has in flight; without that skip a relay-counted id can equal such a request's id
Unverified: the PR1057-R3 witnesses in tests/process/relay-wake-proxy.test.ts drive the relay in-process against a stand-in daemon behind the reattach door; no real Claude Code client and no real agentcpd was run through the relay with the messaging variables absent or partial
